# What gmad must not pack. This is gmad's own ignore file, read when it
# builds the .gma from this folder.
#
# gmad matches a pattern anywhere in the path, so "src" would have taken
# data_static with it. A pattern is a path here, not a fragment.
#
# The addon manifest (addon.json) carries the same list for the publisher.
# Both have to say it, because they are two different tools: the publisher
# reads one, gmad reads this one.
#
# The version stamp is NOT ignored: it is generated, and it is what says
# which commit the .gma was built from.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
*.md
*.psd
src/
opencode.json
packs/example
*.gma
powersoft_k*_data_en_v2.5.html
powersoft_k*_data_en_v2.5_files
